rm Werewolf of Ancient Hunger.", "Westvale Cult Leader's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures you control.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, create a 1/1 white and black Human Cleric creature token.", 'When Byway Courier dies, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', 'When Drownyard Explorers enters the battlefield, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', 'When Drunau Corpse Trawler enters the battlefield, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\n{2}{B}: Target Zombie gains deathtouch until end of turn.', 'When Fleeting Memories enters the battlefield, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nWhenever you sacrifice a Clue, target player mills three cards.', "When Gibbering Fiend enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, Gibbering Fiend deals 1 damage to that player.", 'When Harvest Hand dies, return it to the battlefield transformed under your control.', 'When Inspiring Captain enters the battlefield, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'When Lamplighter of Selhoff enters the battlefield, if you control another Zombie, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', "When Manic Scribe enters the battlefield, each opponent mills three cards.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, that player mills three cards.", "When Obsessive Skinner enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.", 'When Rottenheart Ghoul dies, target player discards a card.', 'When Stoic Builder enters the battlefield, you may return target land card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Stromkirk Mentor enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on another target Vampire you control.', "When Thalia's Lieutenant enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each other Human you control.\\nWhenever another Human enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Thalia's Lieutenant.", 'When Thraben Inspector enters the battlefield, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', "When Tooth Collector enters the battlefield, target creature an opponent controls gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, target creature that player controls gets -1/-1 until end of turn.", "When this creature transforms into Awoken Horror, return all non-Horror creatures to their owners' hands.", 'When this creature transforms into Demon-Possessed Witch, you may destroy target creature.', 'When this creature transforms into Lunarch Inquisitors, you may exile another target creature until Lunarch Inquisitors leaves the battlefield.', 'When you sacrifice a Clue, transform Daring Sleuth.', 'Whenever Bloodmad Vampire deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nMadness {1}{R} (If you discard this card, discard it into exile. When you do, cast it for its madness cost or put it into your graveyard.)', 'Whenever Briarbridge Patrol deals damage to one or more creatures, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nAt the beginning of each end step, if you sacrificed three or more Clues this turn, you may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', 'Whenever Flameheart Werewolf blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Flameheart Werewolf deals 2 damage to that creature.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Flameheart Werewolf.', 'Whenever Kessig Forgemaster blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Kessig Forgemaster deals 1 damage to that creature.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Kessig Forgemaster.', 'Whenever Pious Evangel or another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice another permanent: Transform Pious Evangel.', 'Whenever Wayward Disciple or another creature you control dies, target opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', "Whenever Wolf of Devil's Breach attacks, you may pay {1}{R} and discard a card. If you do, Wolf of Devil's Breach deals damage to target creature or planeswalker equal to the discarded card's mana value.", 'Whenever a Werewolf enters the battlefield under your control, you may transform it.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Vildin-Pack Alpha.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield, if it entered from your graveyard or you cast it from your graveyard, return Prized Amalgam from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nWhenever you sacrifice a Clue, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.', 'Whenever a permanent you control transforms into a non-Human creature, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell during your turn, draw a card.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Hermit of the Natterknolls.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell during your turn, draw two cards.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Lone Wolf of the Natterknolls.', 'Whenever another creature you control dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Unruly Mob.', 'Whenever one or more creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\n{1}{G}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Investigate. You gain 2 life.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, Cathar\'s Companion gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell from your hand, you may cast target card with the same name as that spell from your graveyard. (You still pay its costs.)', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', 'Whenever you sacrifice a Clue, you gain 3 life.', 'Woodland Stream enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'You gain 5 life.', '[+1]: Creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain trample until end of turn.\\n[−1]: Arlinn, Embraced by the Moon deals 3 damage to any target. Transform Arlinn, Embraced by the Moon.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control have haste and \'{T}: This creature deals damage equal to its power to any target.\'"', '[+1]: Reveal the top card of your library and put that card into your hand. Each opponent loses life equal to its mana value.\\n[−X]: Sorin, Grim Nemesis deals X damage to target creature or planeswalker and you gain X life.\\n[−9]: Create a number of 1/1 black Vampire Knight creature tokens with lifelink equal to the highest life total among all players.', '[+1]: Scry 1, then draw a card.\\n[−2]: Return target creature to its owner\'s hand.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "Whenever an opponent casts their first spell each turn, counter that spell."', '[+1]: Until end of turn, up to one target creature gets +2/+2 and gains vigilance and haste.\\n[0]: Create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token. Transform Arlinn Kord.', '[+2]: You may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\\n[−2]: Exile target enchantment, tapped artifact, or tapped creature.\\n[−8]: Search your library for an artifact or creature card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. It gains haste. Return it to your hand at the beginning of the next end step.', '{1}, Discard a card: Create a 1/1 black Vampire Knight creature token with lifelink. Activate only once each turn.', '{1}, Discard a card: Transform Elusive Tormentor.', '{1}, {T}: Put a charge counter on Brain in a Jar, then you may cast an instant or sorcery spell with mana value equal to the number of charge counters on Brain in a Jar from your hand without paying its mana cost.\\n{3}, {T}, Remove X charge counters from Brain in a Jar: Scry X.', '{1}{B}, Sacrifice Vessel of Malignity: Target opponent exiles two cards from their hand. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Vessel of Nascency: Reveal the top four cards of your library. You may put an artifact, creature, enchantment, land, or planeswalker card from among them into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', '{1}{G}: Return target basic land card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{1}{R}, Sacrifice Vessel of Volatility: Add {R}{R}{R}{R}.', '{1}{W}, Exile Dauntless Cathar from your graveyard: Create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{2}: Put target card from your graveyard on the bottom of your library.', '{2}{B}, Discard two cards: Return Ghoulsteed from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', '{2}{B}: Return Sanitarium Skeleton from your graveyard to your hand.', '{2}{G}: Look at the top three cards of your library. You may reveal a creature card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Duskwatch Recruiter.', '{2}{W}, Sacrifice Vessel of Ephemera: Create two 1/1 white Spirit creature tokens with flying.', '{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Explosive Apparatus: It deals 2 damage to any target.', "{3}{B}, Exile Ghoulcaller's Accomplice from your graveyard: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{3}{W}: Target Human gains double strike until end of turn.', '{5}{G}: Quilled Wolf gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', '{B}, Pay 1 life, Mill a card, Discard a card, Sacrifice Sinister Concoction: Destroy target creature.', '{B}: Mill a card.\\nDelirium — At the beginning of your end step, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, transform Autumnal Gloom.', '{T}, Discard a card: Tap target creature.', '{T}, Tap an untapped creature you control: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}, Tap an untapped creature you control: Transform Town Gossipmonger.', '{T}: Add {B} or {G}.\\nDelirium — Deathcap Cultivator has deathtouch as long as there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Warped Landscape: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}: Return Drownyard Temple from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{5}, {T}, Pay 1 life: Create a 1/1 white and black Human Cleric creature token.\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice five creatures: Transform Westvale Abbey, then untap it.', '{T}: Target player draws a card, then discards a card.', '{U}, Sacrifice Vessel of Paramnesia: Target player mills three cards. Draw a card.']
flavor: ['"\'I\'m certain that the fate of Markov Manor is connected to these cryptoliths . . .\' This Tamiyo was on to something."', '". . . and I will prove my devotion."', '"A slayer gets by on wits and reflexes."\\n—Higa, slayer-captain of Gatstaf', '"Ah, to be young again."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"Amazing, isn\'t it, how scraps can come together to create such a wonder?"\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"An unexpected ally."\\n—Rem Karolus, Slayer of Angels', '"Angels and inquisitors terrorize villages, but no one seems to notice the stirring out at sea."', '"As Zendikar has bled, so will Innistrad. As I have wept, so will Sorin."\\n—Nahiri', '"As we muster for war, I have little patience for lethargy or recalcitrance."', '"Children, where are your parents?"\\n—Reig, wandering monk, last words', '"Days ago, you came to my door asking for help, Jace. Yet now here you are with accusations?"', '"Dear brother, it\'s sweet that you have chosen to share your toys with Ludevic, but I too have found some new playmates."\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"Dungeons and cages offer far too little sport."\\n—Relio Voldaren', '"Every answer seems to lead to a more terrifying question."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"Halana grew brambles to create a barricade around our camp, hoping that it would keep the wolves out. That was a mistake for which we almost paid dearly."\\n—Alena, trapper of Kessig', '"How can werewolves be considered abominations next to such creatures?"\\n—Arlinn Kord', '"How do I know where aid is needed? Look around you."', '"I am an instrument of the church wielded against Avacyn\'s enemies."', '"I am not its master. We are of the same pack."\\n—Ulrich, Krallenhorde alpha', '"I have given my life to the church, my soul to Avacyn, and my heart to the people."', '"I have seen it. Seen the end, seen the beginning, the beginning of the end. Not death, no, no. Transcendence!"', '"I have yet to find my equal."', '"I know a ranger that thought to make a cloak of its hide. He ended up losing an eye for his trouble."\\n—Raf Gyel of the Quiver of Kessig', '"I\'m afraid it\'s bad news."', '"I\'m not afraid out here, for I know that a higher power protects me."', '"I\'m sure you have a story. Everyone has a story. You can tell it to the bars."', '"I\'ve never known dryads to suffer visitors in their woods. Beware the Ulvenwald when she welcomes you."\\n—Alena, trapper of Kessig', '"If you refuse to see the light, then you will feel it."', '"If you\'re not surrounded by decadence, my question to you is—why not?"', '"If you\'ve been at this as long as I have, nothing can surprise you. That\'s the hope, at least."', '"In terms of intelligence, homunculi are somewhere between humans and skaabs—clever enough to follow more complex orders, but dim enough to not question them."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"Is this what you found, Tamiyo?"\\n—Jace Beleren', '"It came on as quickly as taking in a breath of air. Cathars who had fought shoulder to shoulder were at each other\'s throats. They were not themselves."\\n—Halmig, Order of Saint Traft', '"It looks like you could use some protection of your own."', '"It seemed so real!"', '"It serves as evidence of the ancient power of the deep, a reminder that the sea is the only thing worthy of reverence."\\n—Runo Stromkirk', '"It\'s right to fear those that you keep locked away."\\n—Rahilda, Vildin-Pack alpha', '"Its previous owners had some stories to share, I\'m certain."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"Just a collage of images: cryptoliths, the sea, a tangle of shipwrecks."', '"Let the flames ignore the sinless."', '"Lost in the woods" is an optimistic way to describe a villager\'s disappearance. "Found in the woods" is frequently more appropriate.', '"Ludevic\'s laboratory is a veritable wonderland. I have never felt so inspired."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"Making a living in Kessig is hard, but I\'ve learned some tricks of the trade."', '"Manners are for mortals."', '"Metamorphosis is a process."\\n—Laboratory notes', '"My earliest work escapes me."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"My faith guides my hand . . ."', '"Never flinch from the truth."\\n—Thalia, Guardian of Thraben', '"No emergency is so dire that it cannot be dealt with elegantly."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"No matter the cost, I must discover the source of these strange happenings."', '"Nothing will cool the fire in their blood. They are too far gone. We must keep them away from our towns at any cost."\\n—Cosper Lowe of the Silbern Guard', '"Once Avacyn returned, I hoped I\'d never need these things again. I didn\'t think I\'d be dusting them off to use against angels."', '"Once in the box, we\'re all the same."', '"Only the pure stand tall in the light."\\n—Sigarda', '"Our enemies will soon discover that we are not as meek as they had believed."', '"Patient complained of burning sensation in upper back and at base of neck. Bed rest recommended. In a couple days, he should feel like a new man."\\n—Lagra, hamlet physician', '"Prayers can be powerful, but I prefer to put faith in my own two hands."', '"Prayers will curdle on the tongue and be heard by rotting ears."\\n—Minaldra, the Vizag Atum', '"Reflect upon your evils lest they reflect upon you."\\n—Inquisitor Laerin', '"She even had the audacity to criticize my wares as inferior."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"Shield yourself with faith. Arm yourself with silver."\\n—Slayer Kastinne', '"So much for neighborly hospitality!"', '"Soft dirt makes for light work."', '"Sometimes it\'s best for the lost to stay lost."\\n—Herzag, mayor of Havengul', '"Sorin, I\'m going to take everything from you."', '"Souls are volatile things. When compressed and loaded into a handheld device, their destructive potential is quite impressive."\\n—Dierk, geistmage', '"Such a beautiful place for a stroll."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Thank you. This blade becomes so hot in my hand, but your blood has quenched it."', '"The appearance of these warped stones throughout the provinces is too pervasive to be random. More evidence is needed to determine the reason behind them."\\n—Tamiyo\'s journal', '"The call of the Blessed Sleep is not so strong as the call to protect those in need."\\n—Saint Traft', '"The city is overrun. I would say burn it to the ground, but that won\'t be necessary."\\n—Inquisitor Delmund', '"The clues have begun to reveal a truth I hesitate to accept."', '"The cornfields promise a good yield this season."\\n—Radwick, farmer of Gatstaf', '"The element of surprise only works when it\'s backed up by a bolt between the eyes."', '"The harder they try to extinguish my faith, the brighter it burns in the darkness."', '"The ravings of the mad are laced with eldritch knowledge."', '"The tides have begun to ignore the moon."\\n—Tamiyo\'s journal', '"The voice has grown louder, its accusations angrier and more insistent. By morning, it will likely drown out all else. I fear what I will do."\\n—Letter discovered in an abandoned estate', '"Their keen sense of smell draws them to the unnatural. To find one is a boon."\\n—Veka, hinterland inspector', '"There is a rich history in a blade like this."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"There is no place like a rooftop laboratory in a lightning storm. It\'s where genius strikes."\\n—Renna, Selhoff alchemist', '"There was a time when the purpose of the church was to heal and protect. I would see that time return."', '"There\'s a forester lives up in the highlands. Tried to sell her one of my finest axes at a bargain, but she wasn\'t interested."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"There\'s not enough salt in all of Nephalia to wither that thing."\\n—Ghoulcaller Enslow', '"There\'s nothing to worry about."', '"They left in one piece. I can\'t speak to how they arrived."\\n—Rupirk, porter at the Rusted Anchor Inn', '"They\'re in the walls! Can\'t you hear them?"', '"This is as far as I go."\\n—Beckram, Skiltfolk escort', '"This is it! All the cryptoliths point here!"\\n—Jace Beleren', '"Those who aren\'t welcome will know it!"\\n—Kolman, elder of Gatstaf', '"To be honest, I\'m not quite sure what\'s going to happen."\\n—Renna, Selhoff alchemist', '"To die failing to save a loved one is just so sad—or, more to the point, pathetic."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Unwavering and loyal, they represent stability in uncertain times."\\n—Rem Karolus, Slayer of Angels', '"Victim discovered at dawn with mouth agape and eyes bulging. No evidence of blood loss or dismemberment. Severe bruising around the neck."\\n—Vallon, Thraben inspector', '"We come bearing the tools of confession and absolution."', '"We come bearing the word of Avacyn and the Lunarch Council."', '"We fight not for Avacyn, but for her ideals; not for the church, but for its people."\\n—Thalia, Guardian of Thraben', '"We must save you from yourselves."', '"We pray to Avacyn on high. On snow-white wings fearless you fly. Keep safe our souls. Keep safe our lives. May angels watch us from the skies."\\n—Children\'s prayer', '"What\'s worse than being alone on the moors at night? Try *not* being alone."\\n—Nadila Maas, moor chaplain', '"When I was a child, we worried about picking the wrong mushrooms for the cook pot. Now we must worry about being picked ourselves."\\n—Halana, Kessig ranger', '"When all else fails, follow the geist\'s lantern."\\n—Vallon, Thraben inspector', '"When the leaves fall and the nights grow cold, look elsewhere for firewood."\\n—Ola of Lambholt', '"Where has little Gossamer gone?"\\n—Thaniel, Gatstaf shepherd', '"While the church thinks in terms of legacies, others think in terms of eternities."', '"Wings that once bore hope are now stained with blood. She is our guardian no longer."\\n—Grete, cathar apostate', '"Write everything down. Trust me."\\n—Vallon, Thraben inspector', '"You must pay for your sin in blood."', '"You should have seen the look on *both* their faces."\\n—Morkamp, Lambholt innkeeper', '"You sought to anger me, Nahiri. Soon you will see how well you have succeeded."', '"You\'ll never believe what I heard."', '"Your recent work is an inspiration. I have the utmost respect for your approach, and your craft is impeccable. At your convenience, I would be honored to collaborate on a project."\\n—Ludevic, letter to Geralf', ". . . but he'll have you for lunch.", 'A good courier travels fast and asks no questions.', "A haunted fog known as the Nebelgast shrouds the cities along Nephalia's coast.", 'A slow knock at midnight is best left unanswered.', 'A spirit is both fettered and free—bound in some ways to its previous existence, yet able to transcend much of the corporeal.', 'Above the cries, a phrase rang out: "You will all be saved."', 'Among vampires, there has long been the belief that the urge to feed must be balanced by the poise of nobility.', 'An old family recipe for an old family grudge.', "As you hear it baying in the distance, you'll feel its breath on your neck.", "At Sorin's appeal, Olivia Voldaren summoned the full might of her bloodline to gather at Lurenbraum Fortress.", "Bear the weight of so many spirits and you'll surrender civility and restraint to savagery and instinct.", 'Being engulfed is just the beginning of the nightmare.', "Courage alone won't keep you alive.", 'Devils sow chaos and reap panic.', "Each cryptolith twists the plane's mana, bending its flow to a singular purpose.", 'Echoing hoofbeats can no longer be assumed to be help from the Gavony Riders.', "Entry 434: There's more to Avacyn's madness . . .", 'Everyone has something to hide.', 'Fear the patient devil, the one who is calm in the midst of chaos. Beware the silent devil, the one whose cackle does not mingle with the others.', 'For some customers, the old apothecary shop still opens its doors.', "For stitchers and necro-alchemists, it's important that work can continue at all hours.", 'From the jagged peaks of Stensia, to the tangled woods of Kessig, to the bogs of Nephalia, the Gavony Riders prepare for all terrain.', 'From within its prison, the book endlessly whispers words of cruelty and spite.', 'Geists seeking redemption must first be given the opportunity.', 'Having infiltrated the Lunarch Council, the Skirsdag await the perfect moment to strike.', "He can't outrun what he is.", 'He hates company . . .', 'Her reputation inspires both loyalty and adoration.', 'His mind was lost long before his flesh.', 'In Gavony, headstones come only from quarries that have been blessed by chaplains.', 'In the quiet of the Somberwald, new horrors stir.', 'In times of madness, people cling to the familiar, monstrous though it may be.', 'It does no good to bar the gate when the enemy is already inside.', 'It fuels its lanterns by leaching the warmth from its surroundings.', 'It has no apparent purpose or direction. It simply drifts, buoyed by breezes both tangible and otherworldly.', 'It is a grim duty to save the world from those created to protect it.', 'It is all too easy to disturb the Blessed Sleep.', 'It is said that one of the most notorious werewolf howlpacks, the Vildin, only calls those whose hands are already stained with blood.', 'It once served a cathar roadwatcher, patrolling the crossways between villages. Its hooves still carry it along the same path.', "It's not just a feeling—you *are* being watched.", 'Its growl is the crackling and popping of a wildfire untamed.', 'Knight-Inquisitors of Saint Raban delve deep into mysteries best left unexplored.', 'Knocking was simply a formality.', "Liliana is never one to follow someone else's lead.", 'Lost loved ones are never truly gone.', 'Many fields now lie fallow in Gavony, as the oxen have been confiscated to perform other duties.', 'Many names and many memories bound together in grim purpose.', 'Nahiri twisted them in shape and bent them to her will.', 'Nephalia is home to many hard-shelled creatures of unusual size, the largest of which are either avoided or worshipped.', 'New cults rising in Nephalia have found allies in the Stromkirk bloodline, whose progenitor worships ancient and terrible forces.', 'No howl. No snarl. Just the roar of flames.', 'None are more dangerous than those who have already been sentenced to death.', 'Older vampires are usually more cautious than the newly-sired, calling upon ancient magic for which neonates lack patience.', 'On Innistrad, it is seldom wrong to stay indoors.', 'On expeditions through Ashmouth, the hunters of Devilthorn Lodge rely on the cleverness of foxes to counteract the mischief of devils.', 'Only the most skillful riders brave the Breakneck Ride through Kessig.', 'Previously the training center for cathars, the Elgaud Grounds are now used by the Lunarch Inquisition to punish those considered to be heretics.', 'Progress comes at a price.', "Rumors are sparks: gather enough of them and something's going to catch fire.", 'Runechanters engrave their strongest wards on those that protect the church.', 'Scarecrows only go so far in sending the message to stay away.', 'Seagrafs yield an abundance of resources for stitchers and ghoulcallers alike.', "Sent to find Sorin, Jace ventured to the vampire's ancestral home, only to find evidence of a deeper mystery.", 'Silverfurs are the last remaining wolfir.', "Sleep doesn't always mean rest.", 'Some have returned to Hollowhenge, the ruins of Avabruck, to restore the lost capital of Kessig.', 'Some minds bend under pressure. Others break.', 'Sorin had created Avacyn, so it was a cruelty beyond imagining, a pain beyond description, that it fell upon him to end her forever.', 'Spirits disturbed by ghoulcallers become geists driven by restless anger.', 'Spiteful geists rise from the muck of the Farbogs, eager to lure travelers to their doom.', 'Thalia established the Order of Saint Traft in an effort to bring together cathars who would stand against the corruption of the Lunarch Council.', 'The Falkenrath have relinquished all pretense at nobility, losing themselves completely to their all-consuming thirst.', "The Needle's Eye, a seldom-used passage that winds through Stensia's mountains, carries travelers close to Ashmouth—too close, some would argue.", 'The barrier between existence and oblivion is thinner than you know.', 'The cathars realized they had not tracked her—she had led them here.', 'The chant was incomprehensible, but its power was unmistakable.', 'The destruction of Markov Manor made the surviving members of the bloodline more dangerous.', "The final pages of the experiment log were blank. Investigators found it abandoned on a desk in the researcher's lab, open, the pages flipping in the wind from a shattered window.", 'The glow in their eyes reveals more than anger or madness.', 'The harvest is never finished.', "The lineage of Runo Stromkirk is known for producing some of Nephalia's greatest fencing masters.", 'The longest nights are measured not in hours, but in heartbeats.', 'The message was clear to Sorin—Nahiri had paid Markov Manor a visit.', 'The mind can only expand so far before it flies apart.', 'The mind is perfectly capable of creating its own monsters.', 'The old hermit would never say what he fed his mushrooms, and people learned not to ask.', "The renewed howling of werewolves announced the end of the Cursemute—and the beginning of Avacyn's madness.", 'The restless geists of common folk often continue their lifelong labors.', 'The seeds of new life take root in the soil of old.', 'There is an eagerness among the Quiver of Kessig to prove they are the equal of the other cathar orders.', 'There is power in the abyss, in blackness more profound than the darkest dreams.', 'Though the first who raised it in a fit of passion is long dead, the axe still carries memories of bitter scorn.', "Thunder isn't all that follows lightning.", "True peace can't be achieved until everyone else is dead.", 'Two creaking waterwheels herald the approach to Briarbridge through the Ulvenwald.', 'Visit the dead, and they may return the favor.', 'When all logical solutions fail, try an illogical one.', 'When the howl beckons, he cannot resist the urge to join the others.', 'When there were no more crows to scare, it focused its efforts elsewhere.', 'With Griselbrand gone, the Skirsdag eagerly awaited another demon to claim their devotion. Ormendahl did not make them wait long.', 'With the fate of Innistrad uncertain, some seek solace in remote areas.', 'Wolves and werewolves join together for the common cause of the hunt.']
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Alejandro Mirabal', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Ben Maier', 'Bud Cook', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Christine Choi', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darek Zabrocki', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Gaillet', 'David Palumbo', 'David Seguin', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Filip Burburan', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Greg Opalinski', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Iain McCaig', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jakub Kasper', 'Jama Jurabaev', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Kang', 'Jason Rainville', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Jose Cabrera', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Karla Ortiz', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lindsey Look', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Min Yum', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Scott Murphy', 'Sean Sevestre', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Tianhua X', 'Titus Lunter', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zoltan Boros']
